Image: evo-flight-lab:sealed; linux/arm64; network none.
No source was modified, initialized, or removed from the original population.

The source declares automatic int adata[9] at line 55 without an initializer.
main passes its address to msum_i4 at line 59. The first loop iteration reads
*base at line 43 in result += *base before any write to adata.

GCC-14 Debian 14.2.0-19:
  gcc-14 -std=gnu11 -O1 -Wall -Wextra -fanalyzer -c SOURCE -o /tmp/gcc.o
Exit 0, warning at 43:19:
  use of uninitialized value '*base' [-Wanalyzer-use-of-uninitialized-value]
The analyzer trace identifies the stack declaration and call from main.

Clang-19 Debian 19.1.7:
  clang-19 --analyze -std=gnu11 -O1 -Xanalyzer -analyzer-output=text
    SOURCE -o /tmp/analysis.plist
Exit 0, warning at 43:9:
  Assigned value is garbage or undefined [core.uninitialized.Assign]
The analyzer trace enters msum_i4 from main and takes the first read.

